    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "What was going through your mind, or what kind of feeling did you have, that made it so hard to stop jerking the controls?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S022",
      "patient_response": "Well... it's awfully embarrassing to try and explain, to be honest with you. I hope you don't think I'm losing my marbles or anything. \n\nIt was just... I had this 'new pattern' figured out, you see? And once I climbed up there during my talk and started jerking the levers to show the crowd... it was like I just had to keep doing it. I don't exactly know how to describe the feeling, but even with everybody hollering at me to get down, I just... I couldn't seem to make my hands quit moving those controls. It was like my body was just stuck doing it, if that makes any sense? \n\nI know it must have looked so foolish for a man my age to be acting like that. I really do try to be a good, respectable representative for the agricultural board, I promise you. Do you... do you think maybe I was just a little overly excited?",
